  "step_3": "The decision reason considers probability differences negligible and prefers the lottery with the higher maximum outcome. The individual in the verbal report acknowledges the 5% probability difference but consciously decides to 'risk' or accept this difference because of the higher gain (1000 Euros more) and absence of downside risk. This aligns with treating the probability difference as unimportant and prioritizing the better maximum outcome. The information considered (maximum outcomes, probability difference) and the justification (accepting lower probability for higher gain due to no downside) match the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual’s reasoning closely follows the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
